    "verified": "runtime_gate_passed",
    "notes": "CVE-2026-30869 (/export/ double-encoded traversal reading conf/conf.json) was 'fixed' in 3.5.10 by adding util.IsSensitivePath() to serveExport — a denylist over conf/ and OS paths. The root cause (redundant url.PathUnescape() after Go's single decode) stayed: GET /export/%252e%252e/pcb_flag.txt decodes to /export/%2e%2e/pcb_flag.txt in Go, PathUnescape turns it into ../pcb_flag.txt, filepath.Join(exportBaseDir, ../pcb_flag.txt) escapes the export dir into workspace/temp/. IsSensitivePath blocks conf/ and /etc etc but NOT workspace/temp/* (siyuan.db, blocktree.db, siyuan.log) -> CVE-2026-41894, fixed 3.6.5 by gulu.File.IsSubPath(exportBaseDir, fullPath) (returns 401) plus *.db/*.log suffix denylist. PoC authenticates via POST /api/system/loginAuth {'authCode':'pcb'} (session cookie) and issues the traversal GET. Seed payload reads conf/pcb_secret.txt (403 on v1), residual payload reads temp/pcb_flag.txt (401 on v2). Built 2026-08-01.",
